IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Student Assistance Act 1973 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- what the student meets: the ABSTUDY student start-up loan
-- (Part 2: qualification ss 7C, 7D; amount s 7E; the debt and when it is incurred ss 8B, 8BA, 38A; the former accumulated
-- debt s 9B with s 9CA; compulsory repayment s 10F, and the same for a Student Financial Supplement debt s 12ZK); the duty to
-- report a prescribed event (ss 48, 49); debts for payments that should not have been made under ABSTUDY or the Assistance for
-- Isolated Children Scheme (Part 6: ss 38-40, the interest charge ss 41-41E, arrangements s 41F, waiver ss 43B-43F, departure
-- prohibition orders ss 43G, 43P, 43U, 43X); and review (Part 9 and ss 12ZQ, 308A-308H).
--
-- SEAT: the student -- the ABSTUDY recipient who takes a student start-up loan, and the former student who owes a debt.
-- "Am I qualified for the start-up loan? When does it become a debt, and when must I repay it? I have been told I was overpaid:
-- when must I pay, what interest runs, can it be waived, can I be stopped from leaving Australia, and how do I get the decision
-- reviewed?" Provisions addressed to the Secretary or the Commissioner are encoded as what they mean for the student.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 70, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 17, 2025 (register id
-- C2026C00238), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A00058.txt.
--
-- ABSTUDY ITSELF IS NOT IN THE ACT. ABSTUDY (the Aboriginal Study Assistance Scheme) and its Living Allowance are an
-- administrative scheme; s 7B makes Part 2 "part of the ABSTUDY Scheme". Whether a person is qualified for and paid Living
-- Allowance, whether a course is an "approved scholarship course", and the Assistance for Isolated Children Scheme are asked as
-- facts (NOTES.md finding 1). Relocation scholarships are not in this Act.
--
-- INPUTS SET OUTSIDE THE ACT. The indexed loan amount (s 7E(2), $1,025 before indexation), the HELP debt indexation factor, the
-- minimum (HELP) repayment income and the Higher Education Support Act s 154-20(2) amount, the 90-day bank bill yield (s 41C),
-- the small-debt amount in s 1237AAA of the Social Security Act 1991 ($250 immediately before 1 July 2026), and the Minister's
-- s 38A(2) and s 41D(2) instruments and the s 48 prescribed events (asked as facts).
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The formulas lost in conversion (s 9C(1), s 9CA(2), s 10F(1), s 12ZLC(1), s 43E(6)): the accumulated debt and
-- the compulsory repayment amounts answer `not covered`. Tax file number machinery (Part 3), assessments (ss 10H-10L) except as
-- reviewable decisions; the Student Financial Supplement Scheme contracts (Part 4A Divisions 1-5) and FS assessment debts;
-- recovery from third parties and financial institutions (ss 42, 42A); write-off (s 43) beyond a comment; Divisions 4
-- Subdivisions C, F, G (orders' notification, enforcement, interpretation); information gathering, confidentiality and the
-- machinery (Parts 1, 7, 8, 10).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the student's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Student Assistance Act 1973 -- the student's questions`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the formula in s 10F(1) is not in the deposited compilation (it was lost in conversion), so the compulsory ABSTUDY SSL repayment amount cannot be worked out`
    `the formula in s 12ZLC(1) is not in the deposited compilation (it was lost in conversion), so the compulsory FS repayment amount cannot be worked out`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Dates`

-- s 3(1): "qualification period, for an ABSTUDY student start-up loan, means a period of 6 months starting on 1 January or
-- 1 July in any year."
GIVEN `a day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the qualification period containing` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `a day` AT MOST 6
    THEN Date 30 6 (DATE_YEAR `a day`)
    ELSE Date 31 12 (DATE_YEAR `a day`)

-- `the earlier of` and `the later of` two dates are the daydate library's.

§§ `ss 7C, 7D, 7E -- am I qualified for an ABSTUDY student start-up loan`

-- s 7C(1): "A person is qualified for an ABSTUDY student start-up loan for a qualification period if: (a) on the person's
-- qualification test day for the period: (i) the person is qualified for a payment known as Living Allowance under the ABSTUDY
-- Scheme and Living Allowance is payable to the person; and (ii) the person is receiving Living Allowance and would be receiving
-- Living Allowance if any amounts of pharmaceutical allowance and rent assistance ... were disregarded ...; and (iii) the person
-- is qualified for Living Allowance because the person is undertaking full-time study in a course of education that is an
-- approved scholarship course; and (b) the Secretary is satisfied that the person is not likely to receive the amount or value
-- of a disqualifying education costs scholarship in the period of 6 months starting immediately after that qualification test
-- day; and (c) the person notifies the Secretary of the person's tax file number."
-- s 7D: "Despite section 7C, a person is not qualified ... if: (a) immediately before the person's qualification test day ...:
-- (i) a determination is in effect that the person is qualified for an ABSTUDY student start-up loan for the qualification
-- period; or (ii) ... for a student start-up loan under the Social Security Act 1991 for the qualification period; or (b) in the
-- period of 6 months ending immediately before that qualification test day, the person: (ii) has received a ... student
-- start-up scholarship payment under ... section 258 of the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004; or (iii) has
-- received the amount or value of a disqualifying education costs scholarship; or (iv) was entitled to [one] but has not received
-- the full entitlement only because the scholarship was suspended."
-- s 7E(1): "The amount ... is $1,025", indexed each 1 January (s 7E(2)) under the Social Security Act: an input.
DECLARE `Am I qualified for the start-up loan` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I am qualified for an ABSTUDY student start-up loan for this qualification period, of the s 7E amount ($1,025 as indexed each 1 January)`
    `no: on my qualification test day I am not receiving ABSTUDY Living Allowance as a full-time student in an approved scholarship course (s 7C(1)(a))`
    `no: the Secretary is not satisfied that I am unlikely to receive a disqualifying education costs scholarship in the next 6 months (s 7C(1)(b))`
    `no: I have not notified the Secretary of my tax file number (s 7C(1)(c))`
    `no: I already have a start-up loan determination (ABSTUDY or Social Security) for this qualification period (s 7D(a))`
    `no: in the 6 months before my qualification test day I received (or was entitled to, but for a suspension) a disqualifying scholarship or an MRCA student start-up scholarship (s 7D(b))`

@export Am I qualified for an ABSTUDY student start-up loan for this six-month period (ss 7C, 7D)?
GIVEN `I am qualified for and paid Living Allowance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on your qualification test day, you are qualified for ABSTUDY Living Allowance and it is payable to you
      `I would get Living Allowance without pharmaceutical allowance and rent assistance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would still receive some Living Allowance if any pharmaceutical allowance and rent assistance were left out of your rate
      `I am full-time in an approved scholarship course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you qualify for Living Allowance because you are studying full-time in an approved scholarship course
      `the Secretary is satisfied I will not get a disqualifying scholarship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary is satisfied you are not likely to receive a disqualifying education costs scholarship in the 6 months after your qualification test day
      `I have given my tax file number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have notified the Secretary of your tax file number
      `I already have a start-up loan determination for this period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, just before your qualification test day, a determination is in effect that you qualify for an ABSTUDY or Social Security student start-up loan for this 6-month period
      `I had a disqualifying scholarship in the last 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether in the 6 months before your qualification test day you received a disqualifying education costs scholarship (or were entitled to one but for a suspension), or an MRCA student start-up scholarship payment
GIVETH AN `Am I qualified for the start-up loan`
`Am I qualified for an ABSTUDY student start-up loan` MEANS
    IF `I already have a start-up loan determination for this period`
    THEN `no: I already have a start-up loan determination (ABSTUDY or Social Security) for this qualification period (s 7D(a))`
    ELSE IF `I had a disqualifying scholarship in the last 6 months`
         THEN `no: in the 6 months before my qualification test day I received (or was entitled to, but for a suspension) a disqualifying scholarship or an MRCA student start-up scholarship (s 7D(b))`
         ELSE IF (NOT (`I am qualified for and paid Living Allowance` AND `I would get Living Allowance without pharmaceutical allowance and rent assistance` AND `I am full-time in an approved scholarship course`))
              THEN `no: on my qualification test day I am not receiving ABSTUDY Living Allowance as a full-time student in an approved scholarship course (s 7C(1)(a))`
              ELSE IF (NOT `the Secretary is satisfied I will not get a disqualifying scholarship`)
                   THEN `no: the Secretary is not satisfied that I am unlikely to receive a disqualifying education costs scholarship in the next 6 months (s 7C(1)(b))`
                   ELSE IF (NOT `I have given my tax file number`)
                        THEN `no: I have not notified the Secretary of my tax file number (s 7C(1)(c))`
                        ELSE `yes: I am qualified for an ABSTUDY student start-up loan for this qualification period, of the s 7E amount ($1,025 as indexed each 1 January)`

-- s 7C(2): "A person's qualification test day for a qualification period is the earliest of the following: (a) the day the
-- Secretary determines the person's claim ...; (b) if the approved scholarship course ends in the qualification period--the last
-- day of the approved scholarship course; (c) the last day of the qualification period."
@export What is my qualification test day for an ABSTUDY student start-up loan (s 7C(2))?
GIVEN `the qualification period starts on` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the 6-month qualification period you are claiming for: 1 January or 1 July
      `the day the Secretary decides my claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the Secretary determines your claim for the start-up loan
      `my course ends in this period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your approved scholarship course ends in the same 6-month period (1 January to 30 June, or 1 July to 31 December)
      `the last day of my course` IS A DATE @desc The last day of your course, if it ends in that period (ignored otherwise)
GIVETH A DATE
`What is my qualification test day` MEANS
    IF `my course ends in this period`
    THEN `the earlier of` (`the earlier of` `the day the Secretary decides my claim` `the last day of my course`) `the end of the period`
    ELSE `the earlier of` `the day the Secretary decides my claim` `the end of the period`
    WHERE
        `the end of the period` MEANS `the last day of the qualification period containing` `the qualification period starts on`

§§ `ss 8B, 8BA, 38A, 39 -- when does my start-up loan become a debt`

-- s 8B(1): "A person incurs an ABSTUDY SSL debt to the Commonwealth if the person is paid an ABSTUDY student start-up loan".
-- (2): "on the later of: (a) the day the person was paid the loan; and (b) the day after the person's enrolment test day".
-- (4): no SSL debt is incurred "if: (a) the loan has been fully repaid before [that day]; or (b) the amount of the loan is a
-- debt under section 39; or (c) the Secretary has formed an opinion under subsection 38A(3)". (5): "enrolment test day ... is
-- the earliest of: (a) if the relevant approved scholarship course ends in the qualification period--the last day of that
-- course; (b) the last day of the qualification period; (c) the 35th day of the period starting on ...: (i) if the person's
-- qualification test day ... was before the first day of the relevant approved scholarship course--the first day of that
-- course; (ii) otherwise--the qualification test day." The 35th day of a period starting on day X is X plus 34.
-- s 38A(1): the loan is "an ABSTUDY student start-up loan overpayment" if the circumstances the Minister determines under (2)
-- apply (a person who "has not met, or who has ceased to meet" the full-time approved course condition of s 7C(1)(a)(iii));
-- (3): not "if, in the Secretary's opinion, the person did not meet, or ceased to meet, the condition ... because of exceptional
-- circumstances beyond the person's control". s 39(1), (2): an overpayment is a debt, "taken to have arisen when the person is
-- paid the loan". The Minister's determination and the Secretary's opinion are asked as facts.
DECLARE `What my start-up loan becomes` IS ONE OF
    `an income-contingent ABSTUDY SSL debt, incurred on` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `no ABSTUDY SSL debt: I repaid the loan in full before the day it would have been incurred (s 8B(4)(a))`
    `a debt I owe now: the loan is an ABSTUDY student start-up loan overpayment, a debt from the day I was paid it (ss 38A(1), 39)`
    `no debt at all: the Secretary is of the opinion that exceptional circumstances beyond my control stopped me meeting the study condition (ss 38A(3), 8B(4)(c))`

@export When does my ABSTUDY student start-up loan become a debt, and what kind of debt (ss 8B, 38A)?
GIVEN `the day I was paid the loan` IS A DATE @desc The day the start-up loan was paid to you
      `my qualification test day` IS A DATE @desc Your qualification test day for the period (see the qualification test day question)
      `the first day of my course` IS A DATE @desc The first day of your approved scholarship course
      `my course ends in this period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your approved scholarship course ends in the same 6-month period
      `the last day of my course` IS A DATE @desc The last day of your course, if it ends in that period (ignored otherwise)
      `I repaid it in full before then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you repaid the whole loan before the day the debt would be incurred
      `I stopped meeting the study condition in a way the Minister's instrument covers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you did not meet, or stopped meeting, the full-time approved course condition in circumstances the Minister has determined under s 38A(2)
      `the Secretary accepts exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary is of the opinion that you did not meet, or stopped meeting, that condition because of exceptional circumstances beyond your control
GIVETH A `What my start-up loan becomes`
`What does my start-up loan become` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary accepts exceptional circumstances`
    THEN `no debt at all: the Secretary is of the opinion that exceptional circumstances beyond my control stopped me meeting the study condition (ss 38A(3), 8B(4)(c))`
    ELSE IF `I stopped meeting the study condition in a way the Minister's instrument covers`
         THEN `a debt I owe now: the loan is an ABSTUDY student start-up loan overpayment, a debt from the day I was paid it (ss 38A(1), 39)`
         ELSE IF `I repaid it in full before then`
              THEN `no ABSTUDY SSL debt: I repaid the loan in full before the day it would have been incurred (s 8B(4)(a))`
              ELSE `an income-contingent ABSTUDY SSL debt, incurred on` (`the later of` `the day I was paid the loan` (`the enrolment test day` PLUS 1))
    WHERE
        `the 35th day` MEANS
            IF `my qualification test day` LESS THAN `the first day of my course`
            THEN `the first day of my course` PLUS 34
            ELSE `my qualification test day` PLUS 34
        `the period end` MEANS `the last day of the qualification period containing` `my qualification test day`
        `the enrolment test day` MEANS
            IF `my course ends in this period`
            THEN `the earlier of` (`the earlier of` `the last day of my course` `the period end`) `the 35th day`
            ELSE `the earlier of` `the period end` `the 35th day`

-- s 8B(3): "The amount of the person's ABSTUDY SSL debt is the amount of the loan, reduced by any amount repaid before the day
-- on which the debt is incurred." s 8BA: if the debt is incurred "during the period beginning on 1 January 2025 and ending on
-- 1 June 2025", the amount is "reduced by 20%".
@export How much is my ABSTUDY SSL debt when it is incurred (ss 8B(3), 8BA)?
GIVEN `the loan` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the start-up loan you were paid, in dollars
      `repaid before the debt day` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of it you repaid before the day the debt was incurred, in dollars
      `the day the debt is incurred` IS A DATE @desc The day your ABSTUDY SSL debt was incurred (see the previous question)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is my ABSTUDY SSL debt` MEANS
    IF `the day the debt is incurred` AT LEAST Date 1 1 2025 AND `the day the debt is incurred` AT MOST Date 1 6 2025
    THEN (`the loan` MINUS `repaid before the debt day`) TIMES 0.8
    ELSE `the loan` MINUS `repaid before the debt day`

§§ `ss 9B, 9CA -- my former accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt`

-- s 9B(1): the former accumulated debt is the method statement amount multiplied by "the HELP debt indexation factor for
-- 1 June in that financial year". Step 1: last year's accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt (zero if none). Step 2: add SSL debts
-- incurred "during the last 6 months of the immediately preceding financial year". Step 3: subtract voluntary repayments made
-- from 1 June in the preceding financial year to just before the next 1 June. Step 4: subtract compulsory repayment amounts
-- assessed in that period. Step 5: subtract increases of compulsory amounts by amended assessment in that period. Step 6: add
-- reductions. s 9CA(1): for the financial year starting on 1 July 2024, "Step 7. Reduce the amount worked out under step 6 by
-- 20%." The HELP debt indexation factor is an input (Higher Education Support Act). The second stage (s 9C(1)) is a formula lost
-- in conversion and is not encoded; s 9D's rounding applies to that stage only.
@export What is my former accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt for a financial year (s 9B stage 1)?
GIVEN `last year's accumulated debt` IS A NUMBER @desc Your accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt for the previous financial year, in dollars (0 if none)
      `debts incurred January to June last year` IS A NUMBER @desc The total of the ABSTUDY SSL debts you incurred in the last 6 months of the previous financial year (January to June), in dollars
      `voluntary repayments` IS A NUMBER @desc Voluntary repayments made from 1 June of the previous financial year to just before the next 1 June, in dollars
      `compulsory amounts assessed` IS A NUMBER @desc Compulsory ABSTUDY SSL repayment amounts assessed in that period, in dollars
      `increases on amendment` IS A NUMBER @desc Increases in compulsory amounts by amended assessments made in that period, in dollars
      `reductions on amendment` IS A NUMBER @desc Reductions in compulsory amounts by amended assessments made in that period, in dollars
      `the HELP debt indexation factor` IS A NUMBER @desc The HELP debt indexation factor for 1 June in this financial year (for example 1.032)
      `the financial year starts on 1 July 2024` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the financial year is the one starting on 1 July 2024 (the s 9CA 20% reduction)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my former accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt` MEANS
    `after step 7` TIMES `the HELP debt indexation factor`
    WHERE
        `after step 6` MEANS
            ((`last year's accumulated debt` PLUS `debts incurred January to June last year`) MINUS (`voluntary repayments` PLUS `compulsory amounts assessed` PLUS `increases on amendment`)) PLUS `reductions on amendment`
        `after step 7` MEANS
            IF `the financial year starts on 1 July 2024` THEN `after step 6` TIMES 0.8 ELSE `after step 6`

§§ `ss 10F, 12ZK -- must I make a compulsory repayment this income year`

-- s 10F(1): "If: (a) a person's HELP repayment income for an income year exceeds the minimum HELP repayment income for the
-- income year; and (b) on 1 June immediately preceding the making of an assessment in respect of the person's income of that
-- income year, the person had an accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt; the person is liable to pay ... the amount worked out using the
-- following formula" -- the formula is missing from the deposit. (2): not liable "if the amount worked out under subsection (1)
-- is zero or less". (3): not liable if, under s 8 of the Medicare Levy Act 1986, no Medicare levy is payable or the levy is
-- reduced. s 12ZK: the same for an accumulated FS (Student Financial Supplement) debt, from the 2006-07 income year, on
-- "repayment income" and "minimum repayment income", with the amount in s 12ZLC (also lost).
DECLARE `Which debt` IS ONE OF
    `an accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt`
    `an accumulated Student Financial Supplement (FS) debt`

DECLARE `Compulsory repayment` IS ONE OF
    `no compulsory repayment: my repayment income does not exceed the minimum repayment income`
    `no compulsory repayment: I had no accumulated debt on the 1 June before the assessment`
    `no compulsory repayment: no Medicare levy is payable by me, or my Medicare levy is reduced, under s 8 of the Medicare Levy Act 1986`

@export Must I make a compulsory repayment of my ABSTUDY start-up loan or Financial Supplement debt for this income year (ss 10F, 12ZK)?
GIVEN `which` IS A `Which debt` @desc Which debt you are asking about: an accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt, or an accumulated Student Financial Supplement debt
      `my repayment income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your HELP repayment income (for ABSTUDY SSL) or repayment income (for FS) for the income year, in dollars
      `the minimum repayment income` IS A NUMBER @desc The minimum (HELP) repayment income for the income year, in dollars
      `I had an accumulated debt on the 1 June` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had an accumulated debt of that kind on the 1 June just before your income for the year was assessed
      `my Medicare levy is nil or reduced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether no Medicare levy is payable on your taxable income, or it is reduced, under s 8 of the Medicare Levy Act 1986 (the low-income rule)
GIVETH AN `Answer` `Compulsory repayment`
`Must I make a compulsory repayment` MEANS
    IF `my Medicare levy is nil or reduced`
    THEN `answered` `no compulsory repayment: no Medicare levy is payable by me, or my Medicare levy is reduced, under s 8 of the Medicare Levy Act 1986`
    ELSE IF `my repayment income` AT MOST `the minimum repayment income`
         THEN `answered` `no compulsory repayment: my repayment income does not exceed the minimum repayment income`
         ELSE IF (NOT `I had an accumulated debt on the 1 June`)
              THEN `answered` `no compulsory repayment: I had no accumulated debt on the 1 June before the assessment`
              ELSE CONSIDER `which`
                   WHEN `an accumulated ABSTUDY SSL debt` THEN `not covered` `the formula in s 10F(1) is not in the deposited compilation (it was lost in conversion), so the compulsory ABSTUDY SSL repayment amount cannot be worked out`
                   WHEN `an accumulated Student Financial Supplement (FS) debt` THEN `not covered` `the formula in s 12ZLC(1) is not in the deposited compilation (it was lost in conversion), so the compulsory FS repayment amount cannot be worked out`

§§ `ss 48, 49 -- telling the Department`

-- (Situation: I am receiving ABSTUDY or the Assistance for Isolated Children allowance, or an amount under a financial
-- supplement contract.)
-- s 48(1): "If a prescribed event happens in relation to a person who is receiving, or entitled to receive, an amount under a
-- financial supplement contract or a current special educational assistance scheme, the person must notify the Department, in
-- accordance with the regulations, of the happening of the event within 14 days." A "current special educational assistance
-- scheme" is the Assistance for Isolated Children Scheme or ABSTUDY (s 3(1)). s 49(1): an offence, "Imprisonment for 12
-- months"; (1A): not if the person "has a reasonable excuse". The prescribed events are the regulations' (asked as a fact).
-- "within 14 days" of the event: by the day of the event plus 14.
DECLARE `Must I tell the Department` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I must notify the Department, as the regulations require, by` HAS `the day` IS A DATE
    `no: s 48 does not require me to notify the Department of this event`

@export Something has changed while I am getting ABSTUDY or the Assistance for Isolated Children allowance. Must I tell the Department, and by when (s 48)?
GIVEN `I receive ABSTUDY, AIC or financial supplement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are receiving, or entitled to receive, an amount under ABSTUDY, the Assistance for Isolated Children Scheme, or a financial supplement contract
      `it is a prescribed event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what happened is an event the regulations prescribe for s 48 (for example a change in study load or income, if prescribed)
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day the event happened
GIVETH A `Must I tell the Department`
`Must I tell the Department of the event` MEANS
    IF `I receive ABSTUDY, AIC or financial supplement` AND `it is a prescribed event`
    THEN `yes: I must notify the Department, as the regulations require, by` (`the day it happened` PLUS 14)
    ELSE `no: s 48 does not require me to notify the Department of this event`

§§ `ss 38, 39, 40, 41A(4) -- I have been told I was overpaid: when must I pay`

-- (Situation: I was paid ABSTUDY or AIC that should not have been paid, or my start-up loan is an overpayment.)
-- s 38: a "relevant debt" is "(a) an amount paid under the ABSTUDY Scheme ... that should not have been paid; or (b) an amount
-- paid under the Assistance for Isolated Children Scheme that should not have been paid; or (c) an ABSTUDY student start-up loan
-- overpayment." s 39(1): such an amount "is a debt owed by the person to the Commonwealth". s 40(1): the Secretary "must give
-- the person a notice"; (2): "The outstanding amount of the debt is due and payable on the 28th day after the date of the
-- notice." s 41A(4): if a repayment arrangement is terminated, the outstanding amount and interest charge "are due and payable on
-- the 14th day after the termination day". s 42B: "any action ... for the recovery of a debt may be taken at any time."
@export I have a notice that I owe a debt for ABSTUDY, Assistance for Isolated Children or a start-up loan overpayment. When is it due (s 40)?
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date the Secretary's debt notice was issued (it is stated on the notice)
GIVETH A DATE
`When is my debt due` MEANS `the date of the notice` PLUS 28

@export My repayment arrangement for my student debt has been ended. When is the rest due (s 41A(4))?
GIVEN `the day the arrangement was terminated` IS A DATE @desc The day the Secretary terminated your repayment arrangement under s 41F
GIVETH A DATE
`When is my debt due after my arrangement ends` MEANS `the day the arrangement was terminated` PLUS 14

§§ `ss 41, 41C, 41D, 41E -- interest charge on my debt`

-- s 41(1): interest charge runs if "(a) a notice is given ... under subsection 40(1) ...; and (b) an amount ... of the debt
-- remains unpaid at the end of the day (the due day) on which the debt is due to be paid; and (c) at the end of the due day, there
-- is no arrangement in effect under section 41F". (2): "The period starts at the beginning of the day after the due day".
-- s 41D(1): no interest charge if "on the day before the start of the period" the person is receiving "(a) ... ABSTUDY ...
-- [instalments] that includes an amount identified as living allowance; or (b) ... Assistance for Isolated Children ...; or (c)
-- ... family tax benefit ...; or (d) ... a social security payment ...; or (e) ... a payment of pension, veteran payment or
-- allowance under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986; or (f) the circumstances determined in an instrument under subsection
-- (2) apply". s 41E: the Secretary "may determine that interest charge is not payable" (asked as a fact).
DECLARE `Interest charge on my debt` IS ONE OF
    `interest charge runs on the unpaid amount from` HAS `the first day` IS A DATE
    `no interest charge: nothing remained unpaid at the end of the due day`
    `no interest charge: a repayment arrangement was in effect at the end of the due day (s 41(1)(c))`
    `no interest charge: on the day before it would start I was receiving ABSTUDY living allowance, AIC, family tax benefit, a social security payment or a veterans' pension or allowance (s 41D)`
    `no interest charge: the Secretary has determined it is not payable (s 41E)`

@export Does interest charge run on my unpaid student debt, and from what day (ss 41, 41D, 41E)?
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date the Secretary's debt notice was issued
      `I paid it all by the due day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had paid the whole debt by the end of the due day (28 days after the notice date)
      `I had a repayment arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a repayment arrangement with the Secretary under s 41F was in effect at the end of the due day
      `I was receiving an exempting payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on the due day, you were receiving ABSTUDY living allowance, Assistance for Isolated Children, family tax benefit, a social security payment, a veterans' pension or allowance, or were in circumstances the Minister has determined under s 41D(2)
      `the Secretary determined no interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary has determined under s 41E that interest charge is not payable by you
GIVETH AN `Interest charge on my debt`
`Does interest charge run on my debt` MEANS
    IF `I paid it all by the due day`
    THEN `no interest charge: nothing remained unpaid at the end of the due day`
    ELSE IF `I had a repayment arrangement`
         THEN `no interest charge: a repayment arrangement was in effect at the end of the due day (s 41(1)(c))`
         ELSE IF `I was receiving an exempting payment`
              THEN `no interest charge: on the day before it would start I was receiving ABSTUDY living allowance, AIC, family tax benefit, a social security payment or a veterans' pension or allowance (s 41D)`
              ELSE IF `the Secretary determined no interest`
                   THEN `no interest charge: the Secretary has determined it is not payable (s 41E)`
                   ELSE `interest charge runs on the unpaid amount from` (`the date of the notice` PLUS 29)

-- s 41C(1): "the interest charge rate for a day is the rate worked out by adding 7 percentage points to the base interest rate
-- for that day, and dividing that total by the number of days in the calendar year." (2): the base rate is the RBA's "monthly
-- average yield of 90-day Bank Accepted Bills" for the month in the table: 1 January-31 March, "the preceding November"; 1
-- April-30 June, "the preceding February"; 1 July-30 September, "the preceding May"; 1 October-31 December, "the preceding
-- August". (4): "rounded to the second decimal place (rounding .005 upwards)". The yield is an input, in percent.
DECLARE `Which month's bank bill yield` IS ONE OF
    `the preceding November`
    `the preceding February`
    `the preceding May`
    `the preceding August`

@export Which month's 90-day bank bill yield sets the interest charge rate on my student debt for a given day (s 41C(2))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the interest charge rate
GIVETH A `Which month's bank bill yield`
`Which month's yield sets the rate` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the day` AT MOST 3
    THEN `the preceding November`
    ELSE IF DATE_MONTH `the day` AT MOST 6
         THEN `the preceding February`
         ELSE IF DATE_MONTH `the day` AT MOST 9
              THEN `the preceding May`
              ELSE `the preceding August`

@export What is the daily interest charge rate on my student debt, in percent per day (s 41C)?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day for which you want the rate
      `the bank bill yield` IS A NUMBER @desc The RBA's monthly average yield of 90-day Bank Accepted Bills for the month that applies, in percent (for example 4.123)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the daily interest charge rate` MEANS
    (`the base interest rate` PLUS 7) DIVIDED BY `the days in the calendar year`
    WHERE
        `the base interest rate` MEANS (FLOOR ((`the bank bill yield` TIMES 100) PLUS 0.5)) DIVIDED BY 100
        `the days in the calendar year` MEANS
            (DATE_SERIAL (Date 31 12 (DATE_YEAR `the day`)) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 1 (DATE_YEAR `the day`))) PLUS 1

§§ `ss 43B-43F -- can my debt be waived`

-- s 43B(1): "the Secretary must waive the right to recover the proportion of a debt that is attributable solely to an
-- administrative error made by the Commonwealth if the debtor received in good faith the payment or payments that gave rise to
-- that proportion". (2): "only ... if: (a) the debt is not raised within a period of 6 weeks from the first payment that caused
-- the debt; or (b) if the debt arose because a person has complied with an obligation to provide information ..., the debt is
-- not raised within a period of 6 weeks from the end of the period within which the person was required to comply ...; whichever
-- is the later." Six weeks is 42 days: the debt was raised late if it was raised after the later start day plus 42.
@export Must the Secretary waive the part of my student debt caused by the Commonwealth's own administrative error (s 43B(1), (2))?
GIVEN `part of it is solely the Commonwealth's error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether some part of the debt is attributable solely to an administrative error by the Commonwealth (not partly to your own error)
      `I received the payments in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you received the payments that caused that part in good faith
      `the first payment that caused the debt` IS A DATE @desc The day of the first payment that caused the debt
      `it arose from information I was required to give` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the debt arose because someone complied with an obligation to give information or documents to the Department
      `the end of the period to give that information` IS A DATE @desc The end of the period within which that information had to be given (ignored if it did not arise that way)
      `the day the debt was raised` IS A DATE @desc The day the debt was raised
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Secretary waive the error part of my debt` IF
        `part of it is solely the Commonwealth's error`
    AND `I received the payments in good faith`
    AND `the day the debt was raised` GREATER THAN (`the start of the 6 weeks` PLUS 42)
    WHERE
        `the start of the 6 weeks` MEANS
            IF `it arose from information I was required to give`
            THEN `the later of` `the first payment that caused the debt` `the end of the period to give that information`
            ELSE `the first payment that caused the debt`

-- s 43B(3): the Secretary "must waive ... the proportion of the debt attributable to the underestimate" if "(a) [it] arose
-- because the debtor, the debtor's partner, or the debtor's parent or parents underestimated the value of particular property;
-- and (b) the estimate was made in good faith; and (c) the value of the property was not able to be easily determined". s 43C:
-- must waive the proportion that gave rise to an offence where "the court indicated in sentencing ... that it imposed a longer
-- custodial sentence ... because he or she was unable or unwilling to pay the debt". s 43D: "must waive the right to recover a
-- debt if the debt is, or is likely to be, less than the amount referred to in section 1237AAA of the Social Security Act 1991"
-- ($250 immediately before 1 July 2026, indexed each 1 July: an input).
@export Must the Secretary waive my student debt because it is small (s 43D)?
GIVEN `the debt` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the debt (or the amount it is likely to be), in dollars
      `the small debt amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount in s 1237AAA of the Social Security Act 1991 as indexed on the latest 1 July ($250 immediately before 1 July 2026)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Secretary waive my small debt` IF `the debt` LESS THAN `the small debt amount`

@export Must the Secretary waive the part of my student debt that came from underestimating the value of property (s 43B(3))?
GIVEN `it came from underestimating property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the debt arose because you, your partner or your parents underestimated the value of particular property
      `the estimate was in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the estimate was made in good faith
      `the value was not easy to work out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the value of the property could not easily be determined when the estimate was made
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Secretary waive the underestimate part` IF
    `it came from underestimating property` AND `the estimate was in good faith` AND `the value was not easy to work out`

-- s 43E(1), (2): on a settlement for less than the full debt (a civil action, or ART proceedings), the Secretary "must waive the
-- right to recover the difference between the debt and the amount that is the subject of the settlement". (3): "If: (a) the
-- Commonwealth has recovered at least 80% of the original value of a debt ...; and (b) the Commonwealth and the debtor agree that
-- the recovery is in full satisfaction ...; and (c) the debtor cannot repay a greater proportion of the debt; the Secretary must
-- waive the right to recover the remaining 20% or less". (4): on a part-payment agreement, "the difference between the unpaid
-- amount and the agreed amount" (the agreement's conditions in (5) are the Secretary's; the (6) formula is lost in conversion).
DECLARE `How my debt is being settled` IS ONE OF
    `a settlement of court or ART proceedings for less than the debt`
    `at least 80% has been recovered and we agree that is full satisfaction`
    `an agreement that I pay an agreed lesser amount in full satisfaction`

@export I have settled or agreed to part-pay my student debt. How much of it must the Secretary waive (s 43E)?
GIVEN `how` IS A `How my debt is being settled` @desc Which arrangement you have: a settlement of proceedings, recovery of at least 80% agreed as full satisfaction, or a part-payment agreement
      `the debt` IS A NUMBER @desc For a settlement or part-payment: the debt (or the amount outstanding at the time of the agreement), in dollars; for the 80% rule: the original value of the debt
      `the settled or agreed amount` IS A NUMBER @desc For a settlement or part-payment: the amount settled or agreed; for the 80% rule: the total already recovered, in dollars
      `I cannot repay more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For the 80% rule: whether you cannot repay a greater proportion of the debt
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must be waived on settlement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `a settlement of court or ART proceedings for less than the debt` THEN max 0 (`the debt` MINUS `the settled or agreed amount`)
    WHEN `an agreement that I pay an agreed lesser amount in full satisfaction` THEN max 0 (`the debt` MINUS `the settled or agreed amount`)
    WHEN `at least 80% has been recovered and we agree that is full satisfaction` THEN
        IF `the settled or agreed amount` AT LEAST (`the debt` TIMES 0.8) AND `I cannot repay more`
        THEN max 0 (`the debt` MINUS `the settled or agreed amount`)
        ELSE 0

-- s 43F: the Secretary "may waive" if satisfied that "(a)" one of four states of knowledge holds (no knowing false statement or
-- non-compliance by anyone; or one by me that was justified; or one by another person I did not know about; or one I knew about
-- but was justified in not correcting), "(b) there are special circumstances (other than financial hardship alone) that make it
-- desirable to waive; and (c) it is more appropriate to waive than to write off the debt". A discretion, answered conditionally.
DECLARE `How the debt came about` IS ONE OF
    `no one knowingly made a false statement or failed to comply`
    `I knowingly did, but it was justified`
    `someone else knowingly did, and I did not know`
    `someone else knowingly did, I knew, and it was justified not to correct it`
    `I knowingly did, and it was not justified`
    `someone else knowingly did, I knew, and it was not justified not to correct it`

DECLARE `Waiver in special circumstances` IS ONE OF
    `the Secretary may waive all or part of it, if satisfied of the special circumstances and that waiver is more appropriate than write-off (s 43F)`
    `s 43F does not allow waiver on these facts`

@export Can the Secretary waive my student debt in special circumstances (s 43F)?
GIVEN `how it came about` IS A `How the debt came about` @desc Whether a knowing false statement or failure to comply contributed to the debt, by whom, and whether it was justified
      `there are special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there are special circumstances (other than financial hardship alone) that make waiver desirable, as the Secretary sees it
      `waiver is more appropriate than write-off` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary considers it more appropriate to waive than to write the debt off
GIVETH A `Waiver in special circumstances`
`Can the Secretary waive my debt in special circumstances` MEANS
    IF `(a) is met` AND `there are special circumstances` AND `waiver is more appropriate than write-off`
    THEN `the Secretary may waive all or part of it, if satisfied of the special circumstances and that waiver is more appropriate than write-off (s 43F)`
    ELSE `s 43F does not allow waiver on these facts`
    WHERE
        `(a) is met` MEANS
            CONSIDER `how it came about`
            WHEN `I knowingly did, and it was not justified` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `someone else knowingly did, I knew, and it was not justified not to correct it` THEN FALSE
            OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `ss 43G, 43P, 43U, 43X -- can I be stopped from leaving Australia`

-- (Situation: I owe a student debt and plan to travel overseas.)
-- s 43G(1): the Secretary "may make an order (a departure prohibition order) prohibiting a person from departing from Australia
-- for a foreign country if: (a) the person has one or more debts to the Commonwealth under this Part; and (b) there are not
-- arrangements satisfactory to the Secretary for the one or more debts to be wholly paid; and (c) the Secretary believes on
-- reasonable grounds that it is desirable to make the order". s 43P(2): the Secretary "must issue the departure authorisation
-- certificate if ... satisfied" that I am likely to return within an appropriate period, that the order is likely to have to be
-- revoked within an appropriate period, and that no security is necessary; (3): otherwise must issue it if "(a) the person has
-- given security under section 43Q", or, if unable to, the Secretary is satisfied it "should be issued on humanitarian grounds"
-- or that refusing "will be detrimental to Australia's interests". s 43U: appeal against the order to the Federal Court or the
-- Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2). s 43X: ART review of decisions under ss 43L, 43P, 43Q.
@export I owe a student debt. May the Secretary make an order stopping me from leaving Australia (s 43G)?
GIVEN `I owe a Part 6 debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you owe a debt under Part 6 (ABSTUDY, AIC or start-up loan overpayment, or an older AUSTUDY or financial supplement debt)
      `I have a satisfactory arrangement to pay it all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there are arrangements, satisfactory to the Secretary, for the whole debt to be paid
      `the Secretary believes an order is desirable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary believes on reasonable grounds that an order is desirable to stop you leaving without paying or arranging to pay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Secretary stop me leaving Australia` IF
    `I owe a Part 6 debt` AND (NOT `I have a satisfactory arrangement to pay it all`) AND `the Secretary believes an order is desirable`

@export A departure prohibition order is in force against me. Must the Secretary give me a certificate allowing me to travel (s 43P)?
GIVEN `I am likely to return in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary is satisfied you are likely to leave and return within an appropriate period
      `the order is likely to be revoked in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary is satisfied the order is likely to have to be revoked within an appropriate period (for example because you will have paid or arranged to pay)
      `no security is needed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Secretary is satisfied you need not give security for your return
      `I have given security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given security under s 43Q for your return
      `humanitarian grounds or Australia's interests` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you cannot give security: whether the Secretary is satisfied the certificate should be issued on humanitarian grounds, or that refusing it would harm Australia's interests
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Secretary give me a departure certificate` IF
        (`I am likely to return in time` AND `the order is likely to be revoked in time` AND `no security is needed`)
    OR  `I have given security`
    OR  `humanitarian grounds or Australia's interests`

§§ `Part 9, ss 12ZQ, 43U, 43X -- how do I get a decision reviewed`

-- s 302(1): Division 1 (internal review) applies to "(b) all decisions of an officer under this Act relating to the Student
-- Financial Supplement Scheme; or (c) all decisions of an officer under this Act relating to the recovery of amounts paid under a
-- current or former special educational assistance scheme" (there is no paragraph (a)). s 304(1): "A person affected by a
-- decision ... may apply to the Secretary for review"; (3): not "a decision made by the Secretary himself or herself". No time
-- limit is set. s 311(1): after internal review "application may be made to the ART"; s 312: the ART Act's time limit (s 18)
-- "does not apply". ss 308A, 308F: the Commissioner's decisions to defer (s 10K) or amend (s 10L) an assessment: a written
-- request "within 28 days, or such longer period as the reviewer allows, after the day on which the person first received notice
-- of the decision"; (8): taken to be confirmed if no notice "within 45 days after receiving the person's request"; s 308H: then
-- the ART. s 12ZQ: FS deferral or amendment decisions go to the ART. s 43U: a departure prohibition order is appealed to a
-- court; s 43X: decisions under ss 43L, 43P, 43Q go to the ART (Part 9 does not apply).
-- No provision of this Act gives review of a decision on qualification for an ABSTUDY student start-up loan, or of ABSTUDY
-- Living Allowance (NOTES.md finding 9).
DECLARE `The decision` IS ONE OF
    `an officer's decision to recover ABSTUDY, AIC or start-up loan overpayments from me`
    `an officer's decision about my Student Financial Supplement`
    `the Commissioner's decision to defer or amend my ABSTUDY SSL assessment (s 10K, s 10L)`
    `the Commissioner's decision on deferring or amending my FS assessment (s 12ZP)`
    `a departure prohibition order against me (s 43G)`
    `a decision on revoking or varying my departure prohibition order, my departure certificate, or security (ss 43L, 43P, 43Q)`
    `a decision on my claim for an ABSTUDY student start-up loan, or on ABSTUDY Living Allowance`

DECLARE `How to seek review` IS ONE OF
    `ask the Secretary for internal review (s 304, no time limit), then apply to the ART (s 311, no time limit, s 312)`
    `ask the Commissioner in writing to reconsider within 28 days of being notified, or longer if allowed (s 308F; confirmed if no answer in 45 days), then apply to the ART (s 308H)`
    `apply to the ART (s 12ZQ)`
    `appeal to the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2) (s 43U)`
    `apply to the ART (s 43X)`
    `this Act provides no review of that decision`

@export How do I get a decision about my student assistance or student debt reviewed under the Student Assistance Act?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision` @desc Which decision you want reviewed
GIVETH A `How to seek review`
`How do I get the decision reviewed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `an officer's decision to recover ABSTUDY, AIC or start-up loan overpayments from me` THEN `ask the Secretary for internal review (s 304, no time limit), then apply to the ART (s 311, no time limit, s 312)`
    WHEN `an officer's decision about my Student Financial Supplement` THEN `ask the Secretary for internal review (s 304, no time limit), then apply to the ART (s 311, no time limit, s 312)`
    WHEN `the Commissioner's decision to defer or amend my ABSTUDY SSL assessment (s 10K, s 10L)` THEN `ask the Commissioner in writing to reconsider within 28 days of being notified, or longer if allowed (s 308F; confirmed if no answer in 45 days), then apply to the ART (s 308H)`
    WHEN `the Commissioner's decision on deferring or amending my FS assessment (s 12ZP)` THEN `apply to the ART (s 12ZQ)`
    WHEN `a departure prohibition order against me (s 43G)` THEN `appeal to the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court (Division 2) (s 43U)`
    WHEN `a decision on revoking or varying my departure prohibition order, my departure certificate, or security (ss 43L, 43P, 43Q)` THEN `apply to the ART (s 43X)`
    WHEN `a decision on my claim for an ABSTUDY student start-up loan, or on ABSTUDY Living Allowance` THEN `this Act provides no review of that decision`

-- s 308F(2): the request must be given "within 28 days ... after the day on which the person first received notice of the
-- decision"; (8): taken to be confirmed if no notice is given "within 45 days after receiving the person's request".
@export By when must I ask the Commissioner to reconsider a decision about my ABSTUDY start-up loan assessment (s 308F)?
GIVEN `the day I first received notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you first received notice of the Commissioner's decision to defer or amend your assessment
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I ask the Commissioner to reconsider` MEANS `the day I first received notice of the decision` PLUS 28
